**Balancing loyalty and openness**

I’m feeling a tug between staying loyal and being honest, and that makes me uncomfortable. I don't want to waste two more years by remaining silent. Their decision is made, but I still have the chance to make a difference, and I’m going to take it. My initial thought is that fairness doesn’t mean I should solely sacrifice. I believe in speaking up when it's needed, especially if it protects my interests. I won't regret those extra two years.

